<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Revolt of the Comuneros</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1520">1520</a>–<a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as War of the Communities of Castile</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Revolt of the Comuneros was a rising of Castilian towns in 1520–1521 against the new king Charles I, his Flemish advisers and his tax demands after his election as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> and a junta of cities, it was crushed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-villalar">Battle of Villalar</a> in April 1521. Afterwards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cortes-of-castile">Cortes of Castile</a> rarely resisted royal taxation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-comuneros.jpg" alt="Revolt of the Comuneros" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonio Gisbert · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Comuneros.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
